# Global Powerhouse Phase H: Visual & UX standards

## Visual excellence (apply to every UI change)

- **No shortcuts:** No default browser buttons, inputs, or scrollbars. Use Shadcn/UI or project design system exclusively. Consistent padding (p-4 or p-6), rounded corners (rounded-xl or rounded-2xl).
- **Hierarchy:** Use font weights and colors (e.g. Slate-900 vs Slate-500) for a clear path for the eye. Sticky headers and zebra-striping for high-density data (e.g. gradebooks).
- **Micro-interactions:** Use Framer Motion (or equivalent) for status changes (e.g. green pulse when a grade is saved). Slide/fade for step transitions.
- **Empty states:** Never a blank screen. Provide a clear "Empty State" with icon and helpful call-to-action (e.g. "Your schedule is clear for today").
- **Loading:** Skeleton screens, not "Loading..." text.
- **Contextual actions:** Prefer "More" (vertical dots) menus for secondary actions; avoid button clutter.
- **Emotional state:** Before shipping UI, consider the user—e.g. parent (anxious), teacher (in a hurry), admin (overwhelmed). Reduce friction with clear hierarchy and calm colors.

## Master design system (Tailwind)

- **Colors:** Sophisticated Navy or Deep Slate for text/sidebar; single Brand Primary (e.g. Indigo-600 or Violet-600); Success Green, Warning Amber, Destructive Red for status. Base: Slate or Zinc; subtle borders (`border-slate-200`) over heavy shadows.
- **Radii:** `rounded-2xl` (16px) for cards; `rounded-lg` (8px) for buttons. Avoid sharp corners.
- **Shadows:** Very subtle—`shadow-sm` or custom `0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.05)`.
- **Typography:** Inter or Geist Sans; clear hierarchy with font weights and muted text for secondary info.

## Dashboard and lists

- **Bento grid:** Each widget is a self-contained card (white/theme surface, subtle border). Charts use the school's primary brand color when available.
- **Cmd+K / Global search:** Command palette on key pages so admins can jump to any student, teacher, or setting. Breadcrumbs show location (e.g. Academics > Gradebook > Class 10A).
- **Empty states:** Always show an empty state with icon, short message, and primary action instead of a blank table or list.

## Django Admin (Unfold)

- Use Unfold's tabs, conditional fields, and advanced filters in ModelAdmin for long forms.
- Per-tenant branding: when `request.school` is set, inject school logo and primary colors in admin context.
- Bento-style admin index via dashboard_callback when configured.

## Feature gate in UI

- When plan doesn't include a module (e.g. Design Studio, Inventory): show Upgrade Modal or friendly paywall instead of empty/broken screen. No module visible without entitlement check.

## Page fold & scroll standards (3–4 fold rule)

- **Max page length:** 4 viewport folds of primary content. Beyond that → tabs, wizard steps, or numbered pagination.
- **2+ folds:** sticky Back to top + in-page section anchor nav (`.rmc-page-fold-nav` / `.rmc-section-nav` + `data-rmc-section-anchor`).
- **Task UI** (forms, tables, wizards, search results): `data-rmc-scroll-policy="paginate"` — numbered pages only, no infinite scroll.
- **Discovery** (feeds, blogs, galleries): `data-rmc-scroll-policy="discovery"` — lazy load allowed.
- **Gate:** `python scripts/verify_page_fold_standards.py`. Full rule: `.cursor/rules/runmycampus-page-fold-standards.mdc`.

## Pixel-perfect & zero-flaw (navigation, UI, security)

Full mandate: `.cursor/rules/runmycampus-pixel-perfect-zero-flaw.mdc` (always on for templates, static, views, urls).

- **Nav/routing:** Django named URLs + host surfaces; no dead `href="#"`; no menu item dumping users on dashboard root.
- **UI:** `design-tokens.css` + `.rmc-*`; skeletons; page-fold + chromatic gates.
- **Proof before done:** `scan_operator_shell_dead_hrefs.py --strict`, `verify_interaction_integrity_completion.py`, `audit_luxury_ui_surface.py`; Playwright `npm run sweep:abrupt-end` when changing chrome or route maps.

## AUDIT & QUALITY LAWS

Before considering any task done, verify:

- **Tenant Leak Check:** Every DB query must use a tenant scope (e.g. `school_id` filter or `schema_context`). Flag raw SQL or ORM without tenant scope.
- **HTMX Partial Integrity:** Every HTMX response must be a valid partial or full base swap. Check for missing `hx-target` IDs.
- **Localization Audit:** No hardcoded user-facing strings; use `_()` or `{% trans %}`.
- **Offline Sync Gaps:** Every POST/PUT that changes data must have corresponding IndexedDB offline buffering logic where offline is supported.
- **Usage Limit Enforcement:** Before any "Create" action (e.g. new student), verify middleware or decorator enforces the tenant Plan limits (max_students / max_staff).
- **Sentry / logging:** Tag errors with tenant/school context (e.g. `sentry_sdk.set_tag("school_id", school_id)`) so support can filter by tenant.
